Error: Jet.CompoundAssignToIndex: Compound assignment can't target an indexed slot.
  --> compound_index_target.jet:4:11
    |
  4 |     counts["missing"] += 1
    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A compound update reads an indexed slot before it writes; that read can panic when a map key is missing.
 Fix: Give the slot a starting value, such as `map[key, or: 0] += 1`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.CompoundAssignToIndex

Error: Jet.CompoundAssignToIndex: Compound assignment can't target an indexed slot.
  --> compound_index_target.jet:5:11
    |
  5 |     counts["missing"] -= 1
    |           ^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A compound update reads an indexed slot before it writes; that read can panic when a map key is missing.
 Fix: Give the slot a starting value, such as `map[key, or: 0] -= 1`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.CompoundAssignToIndex
